1
00:00:16,590 --> 00:00:20,760
See, Joe, that's why your parents told you not to jump on the bed.

2
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:31,800
# So no one told you life was gonna be this way #

3
00:00:32,370 --> 00:00:36,540
# Your job's a joke, you're broke, your love life's D.O.A. #

4
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:41,260
# It's like you're always stuck in second gear #

5
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:43,820
# When it hasn't been your day, #

6
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:46,820
# your week, your month, or even your year #

7
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:50,780
# but I'll be there for you #

8
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:52,610
# When the rain starts to pour #

9
00:00:52,610 --> 00:00:55,730
# I'll be there for you #

10
00:00:55,730 --> 00:00:57,570
# Like I've been there before #

11
00:00:57,570 --> 00:01:00,580
# I'll be there for you #

12
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:04,240
# 'Cause you're there for me too #

13
00:01:11,650 --> 00:01:14,860
Hey, look at me. I'm making jam.

14
00:01:15,150 --> 00:01:17,280
I've been at it since 4:00 this morning.

15
00:01:17,450 --> 00:01:19,280
Where'd you get fruit at 4 in the morning?

16
00:01:19,490 --> 00:01:20,910
Went down at the docks.

17
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:23,040
Bet you didn't know you can get it wholesale.

18
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:24,910
I didn't know there were docks.

19
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:28,120
Hey.

20
00:01:28,290 --> 00:01:30,080
Aw, is it broken?

21
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:32,800
No, but I gotta wear this thing for a couple weeks.

22
00:01:33,170 --> 00:01:36,090
Did you tell the doctor you did it jumping up and down on your bed?

23
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:40,390
No. I had a whole story worked out, but then...

24
00:01:40,550 --> 00:01:41,850
...Chandler sold me out.

25
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:43,100
I'm sorry, Joe.

26
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:47,020
I didn't think the doctor was gonna buy that it just fell out of his socket.

27
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:50,850
What is this? Fruit?

28
00:01:54,190 --> 00:01:55,360
Monica's making jam.

29
00:01:56,030 --> 00:02:00,410
Jam? I love jam. Hey, how come we never have jam at our place?

30
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:02,740
Because the kids need new shoes.

31
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:07,960
I'm going into business, people. I'm sick of being depressed about Richard.

32
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:10,870
I needed a plan. A plan to get over my man.

33
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:14,090
What's the opposite of man? Jam.

34
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:18,090
Joey, don't. It's way too hot.

35
00:02:25,390 --> 00:02:27,390
This will just be my batch.

36
00:02:45,410 --> 00:02:48,120
Um, that's it. No. Hey you. J. Crew guy...

37
00:02:48,370 --> 00:02:50,120
Yeah. Why are you following me?

38
00:02:50,370 --> 00:02:52,620
All week long, everywhere I look, there's you.

39
00:02:53,130 --> 00:02:55,880
You wouldn't return my calls. You sent back my letters.

40
00:02:56,050 --> 00:02:58,880
- What?     - One more chance, Ursula. Please.

41
00:03:02,550 --> 00:03:03,640
Oh. Well, this is awkward.

42
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,470
Why?

43
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:09,430
Yeah, because you want Ursula, and I'm Phoebe. Twin sisters.

44
00:03:10,890 --> 00:03:12,270
Seriously.

45
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:16,150
Oh. That's great. I'm stalking the wrong woman.

46
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:19,030
I am such a dingus!

47
00:03:19,190 --> 00:03:21,200
Oh, you're not a dingus.

48
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:24,990
I just... I want you to know I didn't used to be like this.

49
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:27,410
Before I met your sister, I was, like, this normal guy...

50
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:29,620
...who sold beepers and cellular phones.

51
00:03:30,370 --> 00:03:34,290
Well... I mean, look, it's not your fault, you know?

52
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:37,250
I mean, this is just what she does to guys, okay?

53
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:38,710
Just...

54
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,470
Well, thanks.

55
00:03:41,630 --> 00:03:43,970
Wait. You know what? I got a little story.

56
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:46,140
When I was in junior high school...

57
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:48,760
...I went through this period where I thought I was a witch.

58
00:03:48,930 --> 00:03:51,640
And there was this guidance counselor who said something to me...

59
00:03:51,810 --> 00:03:53,480
...that I think will help you a lot.

60
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:57,230
He said, "Okay, you're not a witch. You're just an average student."

61
00:03:58,570 --> 00:04:01,360
- See what I'm saying?     - Not really.

62
00:04:02,650 --> 00:04:04,030
Um, well, get over it.

63
00:04:06,950 --> 00:04:10,160
I mean, you just... You seem like a really nice guy.

64
00:04:10,330 --> 00:04:13,830
You know, I just... Don't be so hard on yourself, okay?

65
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:18,210
Wait, you're right. I know you're right. And thanks for being so nice.

66
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:20,550
Here.

67
00:04:21,050 --> 00:04:22,590
Thanks a lot.

68
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:24,840
Do you wanna get a cup of coffee or...?

69
00:04:25,010 --> 00:04:27,010
- Yeah, okay.     - Okay.

70
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:31,350
You don't have to walk behind me anymore.

71
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,560
Sorry.

72
00:04:34,230 --> 00:04:35,890
- Mon?     - Mon?

73
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:41,440
"Gone for more jars. Back later. Monica Geller."

74
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:44,950
Wait a minute. Look.

75
00:04:45,110 --> 00:04:46,740
- Look, look, look.     - What, what, what?

76
00:04:46,910 --> 00:04:49,200
- It's an empty apartment.     - Mm.

77
00:04:49,370 --> 00:04:51,700
We're all alone in an empty apartment.

78
00:04:51,870 --> 00:04:55,910
Aw, honey, come on. I have to be at work in, like, 10 minutes and, oh...

79
00:04:56,750 --> 00:05:01,090
All right. Well, it's not like I'm employee of the year or anything.

80
00:05:06,590 --> 00:05:07,630
There it is.

81
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,760
Oh, that's what you're talking about.

82
00:05:09,930 --> 00:05:11,720
- Hey.     - Hey.

83
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:13,640
Do I look fat?

84
00:05:14,390 --> 00:05:15,770
No.

85
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,940
Okay, I accept that.

86
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:19,900
When Janice asked me and I said no...

87
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:22,980
...she took that to mean that I was calling her a cow.

88
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:27,070
Okay, walk us through it, honey. Walk us through it.

89
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,740
Okay, well, Janice said, uh:

90
00:05:28,910 --> 00:05:31,910
"Hi. Do I look fat today?" And I looked at her...

91
00:05:33,870 --> 00:05:35,540
You looked at her?

92
00:05:38,290 --> 00:05:39,620
You never look.

93
00:05:40,750 --> 00:05:44,960
You just answer. It's like a reflex. "Do I look fat?" "No."

94
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:50,430
"Is she prettier than I am?" "No."

95
00:05:51,470 --> 00:05:52,760
- "Does size matter?"     - No.

96
00:05:52,930 --> 00:05:54,600
And it works both ways.

97
00:05:57,640 --> 00:06:00,850
Okay, so you both just know this stuff?

98
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:04,400
You know, after about 30 or 40 fights, you kind of catch on.

99
00:06:05,860 --> 00:06:07,610
Okay. For instance, ahem:

100
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:12,120
Let's say Janice is coming back from a trip and she gives you two options.

101
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:15,450
Option number one: She'll take a cab home from the airport.

102
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:19,370
Or option two: You can meet her at baggage claim. What do you do?

103
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:20,670
That's easy. Baggage claim.

104
00:06:20,830 --> 00:06:22,750
Ehh! Wrong. Now you're single.

105
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:28,590
It's actually secret option number three.

106
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:32,050
You meet her at the gate. That way she knows you love her.

107
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:34,470
Okay, this is good. This is good.

108
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:38,560
All right, listen, I have one. Janice likes to cuddle...

109
00:06:38,730 --> 00:06:41,020
...at night, which I'm all for.

110
00:06:41,230 --> 00:06:44,980
But, uh, you know, when you want to go to sleep, you want some space.

111
00:06:45,150 --> 00:06:47,980
So, uh, you know, how do I tell her that without...

112
00:06:48,150 --> 00:06:51,240
...you know, accidentally calling her fat or something?

113
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:56,030
Oh. Honey, I'm sorry. We can't help you there, because we're cuddly sleepers.

114
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,160
Okay, I'm late for work.

115
00:06:59,330 --> 00:07:02,830
- Are you guys gonna come down?     - Uh, yeah. I'm right behind you.

116
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,210
- Good luck, Chandler.     - Thank you, Rachel.

117
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:07,050
- Bye, sweetie.     - Bye, honey.

118
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:11,050
Okay, the sleeping thing.

119
00:07:11,970 --> 00:07:14,550
Very tricky business but there is something you can do.

120
00:07:14,970 --> 00:07:17,890
- I thought you were cuddly sleepers.     - No.

121
00:07:19,850 --> 00:07:22,520
No, not cuddly. Not me. Just her.

122
00:07:22,690 --> 00:07:24,940
I'm like you. I need the room. Ahem.

123
00:07:25,110 --> 00:07:27,520
Okay, come here. Ahem.

124
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:32,110
Okay. You're in bed.

125
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:33,610
Yeah?

126
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:39,620
- I'm gonna use the cushion.     - Yeah.

127
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:45,330
Okay. You're in bed. She's over on your side cuddling.

128
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:48,550
Now, you wait for her to drift off...

129
00:07:48,710 --> 00:07:51,210
...and then you hug her...

130
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:56,140
...and roll her over to her side of the bed.

131
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:58,430
And then you...

132
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:02,180
...roll away.

133
00:08:03,190 --> 00:08:05,350
Hug for her.

134
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:10,900
Roll for you.

135
00:08:11,820 --> 00:08:13,740
- Okay, the old "hug and roll."     - Yep.

136
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,990
- Okay. One question.     - Shoot.

137
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:18,530
You're pretending the pillow's a girl, right?

138
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:22,950
Remember when you were a kid...

139
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:25,330
...and your mom would drop you off at the movies...

140
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:28,420
...with a jar ofjam and a little spoon?

141
00:08:31,590 --> 00:08:33,340
You're so pretty.

142
00:08:38,430 --> 00:08:40,390
- Hi.     - Hey, Phoebe.

143
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:44,310
Hey, oh! You know that guy who's been following me? I talked to him today.

144
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:47,150
You talked to him? Are you crazy?

145
00:08:49,150 --> 00:08:52,980
Okay, first, I'm not crazy. And second, say it. Don't spray it.

146
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:57,740
Anyway, his name is Malcolm, and he wasn't following me.

147
00:08:57,950 --> 00:09:00,780
I mean, he was, but just because he thought I was Ursula. Ick.

148
00:09:03,290 --> 00:09:07,330
And that's why... That's why he couldn't just come up and talk to me.

149
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:09,790
Because of the restraining order.

150
00:09:11,670 --> 00:09:14,670
Hmm. Not feeling better about Malcolm.

151
00:09:15,130 --> 00:09:18,390
Oh! No, no, no, he's not like a kook.

152
00:09:18,550 --> 00:09:22,680
No, he's just this, like, very passionate, incredibly romantic guy...

153
00:09:22,850 --> 00:09:25,560
...that just got a teensy bit carried away, you know?

154
00:09:25,730 --> 00:09:28,810
And we just get along really well, and he's so cute.

155
00:09:29,770 --> 00:09:34,900
Oh, my God. You've got a crush on your sister's stalker.

156
00:09:35,070 --> 00:09:38,030
No, I'm just gonna help him, you know, get "de-Ursula-ized."

157
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:41,120
Like, you know... Like I did for Joey after he went out with her.

158
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:43,660
Yeah, but I didn't stalk her. I mean...

159
00:09:43,830 --> 00:09:45,750
I asked for the news, not the weather.

160
00:09:47,830 --> 00:09:50,750
- Hey, guys.     - Hey, Mon.

161
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:54,210
Joey, this is for you. It's blackberry currant.

162
00:09:59,390 --> 00:10:00,550
Yeah.

163
00:10:01,050 --> 00:10:02,850
Hey, Joe, I gotta ask.

164
00:10:03,010 --> 00:10:06,220
The girl from the Xerox place, buck naked...

165
00:10:06,810 --> 00:10:09,350
...or a big tub of jam?

166
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:12,560
Put your hands together.

167
00:10:16,690 --> 00:10:19,240
Joey, take your time with that. That's my last batch.

168
00:10:19,950 --> 00:10:21,450
No more jam?

169
00:10:22,530 --> 00:10:24,580
What happened to your jam plan?

170
00:10:24,830 --> 00:10:28,330
Well, I figured out I'd need to charge 17 bucks a jar just to break even.

171
00:10:28,660 --> 00:10:31,830
So I've got a new plan now. Babies.

172
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:35,500
Well, you're gonna need much bigger jars.

173
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:41,550
- What are you talking about?     - About me having a baby.

174
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:43,760
- Are you serious?     - Yeah.

175
00:10:43,930 --> 00:10:47,640
The great thing about the jam plan was I was take control of my life.

176
00:10:47,810 --> 00:10:50,690
So I asked myself, "What is the most important thing to me?"

177
00:10:50,850 --> 00:10:53,560
And that's when I came up with the baby plan.

178
00:10:53,730 --> 00:10:56,570
Well, aren't you forgetting something?

179
00:10:56,730 --> 00:10:59,940
What is, uh...? What is that guy's name? Dad.

180
00:11:01,410 --> 00:11:04,990
It took me 28 years to find one man that I wanted to spend my life with.

181
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:09,160
If I have to wait another 28 years, then I'll be 56 before I can have a baby.

182
00:11:09,330 --> 00:11:11,330
And that's just stupid.

183
00:11:12,750 --> 00:11:14,750
That's what's stupid?

184
00:11:16,750 --> 00:11:21,260
I don't need an actual man. Just a couple of his best swimmers.

185
00:11:21,590 --> 00:11:25,800
You know? And there are places that you can go to get that stuff.

186
00:11:25,970 --> 00:11:28,010
Down at the docks again?

187
00:11:38,110 --> 00:11:40,780
Night-night, Bing-a-ling.

188
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:43,990
Night-night...

189
00:11:44,820 --> 00:11:46,410
...Janice.

190
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:52,960
Look at all that room on her side.

191
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:55,000
You could fit a giant penguin over there.

192
00:11:57,170 --> 00:11:58,880
That'd be weird, though.

193
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:01,880
Hug and roll time.

194
00:12:02,050 --> 00:12:04,340
I'm hugging. I'm hugging.

195
00:12:04,510 --> 00:12:07,300
You're rolling, and...

196
00:12:07,470 --> 00:12:09,560
Yes! Freedom!

197
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:12,140
Except for this arm.

198
00:12:12,310 --> 00:12:15,060
I'm stuck. Stuck arm.

199
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:19,690
Okay, time for the old tablecloth trick. One fluid motion.

200
00:12:19,860 --> 00:12:21,690
Quick like a cat. Quick like a cat.

201
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:24,990
And one, two...

202
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:26,610
...three.

203
00:12:33,750 --> 00:12:35,000
Here's my binoculars.

204
00:12:35,170 --> 00:12:37,630
Oh, great. Great. You're doing great.

205
00:12:37,790 --> 00:12:41,000
You know, real strong. Going strong. Keep going.

206
00:12:41,590 --> 00:12:43,970
These are my night-vision goggles.

207
00:12:44,970 --> 00:12:48,340
This is the book I pretend to read when I'm watching her in the park.

208
00:12:49,430 --> 00:12:52,470
And these are Madlibs. They're just for fun.

209
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:54,680
Oh, yeah. Ha, ha. What's this?

210
00:12:54,850 --> 00:12:59,560
Oh. This is the log I kept, recording her every movement.

211
00:13:00,190 --> 00:13:03,690
- You want to hear something from it?     - Um, not even a little bit.

212
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:07,160
- It's about you.     - Oh, okay, then.

213
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:15,250
"I met Phoebe today.

214
00:13:15,410 --> 00:13:17,870
She was really nice to me even though I'm such a loser."

215
00:13:20,130 --> 00:13:23,090
"And then when I was walking home, I thought about her a lot.

216
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:26,380
It was weird but kind of cool."

217
00:13:27,550 --> 00:13:28,930
Good. Ha, ha.

218
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:31,720
So, what were you thinking?

219
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:35,730
I was thinking what it'd be like to kiss you.

220
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,060
- Really?     - No.

221
00:13:40,610 --> 00:13:43,900
See, that's just something I said now so that maybe I could kiss you.

222
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:46,320
Oh, okay.

223
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:55,120
No, it's all right. I just had a jar of mustard.

224
00:13:56,580 --> 00:14:01,710
Okay. Sperm donor number 03815, come on down!

225
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:04,590
Okay, he's 6'2", 170 pounds.

226
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:07,800
And he describes himself as a male Geena Davis.

227
00:14:07,970 --> 00:14:10,050
You mean there's more than one of us?

228
00:14:12,140 --> 00:14:15,350
You can't do this, Mon, all right? If you do this, I'm gonna...

229
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:18,310
- You're gonna what?     - I'm gonna tell Mom.

230
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:22,770
Honey, I'm sorry, but he's right. I love you, but you're crazy.

231
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:25,940
- Crazy.     - What? Why? Why is this crazy?

232
00:14:26,110 --> 00:14:28,820
- So this isn't the ideal way to do something...     - Oh, it's not...

233
00:14:28,990 --> 00:14:31,030
Lips moving. Still talking.

234
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:33,830
It may not be ideal...

235
00:14:33,990 --> 00:14:36,290
...but I'm so ready.

236
00:14:36,450 --> 00:14:39,160
You know, I see the way Ben looks at you.

237
00:14:39,620 --> 00:14:41,790
It makes me ache, you know?

238
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,130
Check it out. Jam crackers.

239
00:14:48,380 --> 00:14:50,720
Okay. All right, how's this?

240
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:53,930
Twenty-seven. Italian-American guy.

241
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:55,760
He's an actor.

242
00:14:55,930 --> 00:14:57,680
Born in Queens.

243
00:14:57,850 --> 00:15:01,440
Wow. Big family. Seven sisters...

244
00:15:01,980 --> 00:15:05,190
...and he's the only boy.

245
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:11,910
Oh, my God. Under personal comments: "New York Knicks rule."

246
00:15:12,070 --> 00:15:13,620
Yeah, the Knicks rule.

247
00:15:17,830 --> 00:15:19,660
Joey, this is you.

248
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,500
